/**
@page pixel_formats Pixel Formats and Buffer Sizes

@section format_notation Size Notation

For image width `W` and height `H`, define:

- `P = W * H`
- `CW = (W + 1) / 2`
- `CH = (H + 1) / 2`

The rounded chroma dimensions allow odd `W` and `H`. Applications must perform
checked multiplication before allocating buffers from untrusted dimensions.

@section format_rgb RGB Layouts

| FourCC | Exact byte or plane order | Bytes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| #SGL_FOURCC_RGBA | packed `R, G, B, A` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_ARGB | packed `A, R, G, B` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_BGRA | packed `B, G, R, A` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_ABGR | packed `A, B, G, R` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_RGB | packed `R, G, B` | `3P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_BGR | packed `B, G, R` | `3P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_RGBA_PLANAR | planes `R, G, B, A` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_ARGB_PLANAR | planes `A, R, G, B` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_BGRA_PLANAR | planes `B, G, R, A` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_ABGR_PLANAR | planes `A, B, G, R` | `4P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_RGB_PLANAR | planes `R, G, B` | `3P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_BGR_PLANAR | planes `B, G, R` | `3P` |

The planar RGB identifiers are SGL extensions because DRM/V4L2 do not define
equivalent RGB-only planar FourCC values.

@section format_yuv YUV Layouts

| FourCC | Exact byte or plane order | Bytes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YUV444_PACKED | packed `Y, Cb, Cr` | `3P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YUV444_PLANAR | planes `Y, Cb, Cr` | `3P` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YUYV | groups `Y0, Cb0, Y1, Cr0` | `4 * CW * H` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YVYU | groups `Y0, Cr0, Y1, Cb0` | `4 * CW * H` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_UYVY | groups `Cb0, Y0, Cr0, Y1` | `4 * CW * H` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_VYUY | groups `Cr0, Y0, Cb0, Y1` | `4 * CW * H` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YUV422_PLANAR | `Y` plane, then `Cb`, `Cr` at half width | `P + 2 * CW * H` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_YUV420_PLANAR | `Y` plane, then `Cb`, `Cr` at half width/height | `P + 2 * CW * CH` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_NV12 | `Y` plane, then interleaved `Cb, Cr` | `P + 2 * CW * CH` |
| #SGL_FOURCC_NV21 | `Y` plane, then interleaved `Cr, Cb` | `P + 2 * CW * CH` |

@section format_view Viewing Raw Output

Use ffplay's `rawvideo` demuxer with matching dimensions and pixel format. For
example:

@code{.sh}
ffplay -f rawvideo -pixel_format rgba -video_size 1280x720 frame.raw
ffplay -f rawvideo -pixel_format nv12 -video_size 1280x720 frame.raw
ffplay -f rawvideo -pixel_format yuyv422 -video_size 1280x720 frame.raw
@endcode

ffplay does not expose names for every SGL planar RGB layout. Convert such a
file to a viewer-supported packed layout before display.
*/
